From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 20:41:41 +0200
Subject: MIPS: dts: intel-mips: pin the GPHY IDs

Without a compatible naming the identifier, of_mdiobus_register_phy() has
to go out on the bus and read the identification registers before it can
create the PHY device. The integrated GPHY cores serve those registers from
hardwired logic as soon as the MDIO master is alive, well before the
firmware the SoC loads into them has finished booting, so the scan can
sample a core that is only half awake: MII_BMSR reads back as 0x0000 on a
transaction that reports success, and the abilities derived from it stay
empty for the rest of the boot.

Spelling the identifier out takes the phy_device_create() path instead, so
enumeration issues no bus transaction at all and the PHY device exists
whether or not its core has come up yet. This is also what the vendor
device tree does.

0xd565a409 is what all five cores report on every board using these files;
the driver matches it under an exact mask, and the low bits of the
identifier are set by the firmware variant that was loaded.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/seale_avm.dtsi b/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/seale_avm.dtsi
index 45a3edf47e12..4f99e42af75b 100644
--- a/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/seale_avm.dtsi
+++ b/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/seale_avm.dtsi
@@ -82,20 +82,33 @@ gswip_mdio: gswip-mdio@1c003c10 {
 		 * equals this PHY's MDIO address. Getting the pairing wrong
 		 * gives a working link on the wrong front-panel socket, which
 		 * no probe-time check can catch.
+		 *
+		 * The identifier is spelled out on every node so the PHY device
+		 * is created from the device tree alone. These cores answer
+		 * their ID registers before the firmware the SoC loads has
+		 * finished booting, so a bus scan can sample a half-alive core.
 		 */
 		gphy_lan1: ethernet-phy@5 {
+			compatible = "ethernet-phy-idd565.a409",
+				     "ethernet-phy-ieee802.3-c22";
 			reg = <0x05>;
 		};
 
 		gphy_lan2: ethernet-phy@4 {
+			compatible = "ethernet-phy-idd565.a409",
+				     "ethernet-phy-ieee802.3-c22";
 			reg = <0x04>;
 		};
 
 		gphy_lan3: ethernet-phy@3 {
+			compatible = "ethernet-phy-idd565.a409",
+				     "ethernet-phy-ieee802.3-c22";
 			reg = <0x03>;
 		};
 
 		gphy_lan4: ethernet-phy@2 {
+			compatible = "ethernet-phy-idd565.a409",
+				     "ethernet-phy-ieee802.3-c22";
 			reg = <0x02>;
 		};
 	};
diff --git a/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/seale_avm_grx550.dtsi b/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/seale_avm_grx550.dtsi
index 1a27ac69965e..a2ec4dac78a5 100644
--- a/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/seale_avm_grx550.dtsi
+++ b/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/seale_avm_grx550.dtsi
@@ -49,6 +49,8 @@ gswr_mdio: gswip-mdio@1a003c10 {
 		status = "okay";
 
 		gphy_wan: ethernet-phy@1 {
+			compatible = "ethernet-phy-idd565.a409",
+				     "ethernet-phy-ieee802.3-c22";
 			reg = <0x01>;
 		};
 	};
